# pr-444: gh-443: basename headers instead of <file path=...> wrappers in instruction embedding

## Description

Closes #443.

`InstructionProcessor._embedFilePaths` wrapped every inlined file in `<file path="...">`...`</file>` with the FULL path — on a runner that is the absolute pack path (`/home/runner/.dmtools/packs/pr_rework-0.1.183/.../`), ~110 chars × ~9 files of dead weight in every combined agent prompt (live: dart #441 rework prompt, 22358 bytes).

Now each embedded file gets a one-line `## <basename>` header: cross-file references ('see tdd_approach.md') still resolve, no absolute paths, no closing tags. Java-core parity: the Java InstructionProcessor already inlines bare content — same token cost, plus the navigability header.

Tests updated: embedding asserts the basename header and the ABSENCE of the old wrapper (both suites green, 21 cases).
